RenHDrum 0.6.0, the upstream release binary
https://github.com/trzz1214/RenHDrum/tree/v0.6.0
https://github.com/trzz1214/RenHDrum/releases/tag/v0.6.0

The build links the C runtime statically (.cargo/config.toml sets
-C target-feature=+crt-static for x86_64-pc-windows-msvc), so the release binary is
shipped here as it is: no rebuild is needed for players without the Visual C++
redistributable. renhdrum.dll is the release asset byte for byte (915456 bytes), and its
sha256 matches the one on the release page. Its dependencies:

    api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0.dll
    KERNEL32.dll
    ntdll.dll

No VCRUNTIME140.dll, no MSVCP140.dll, no api-ms-win-crt-*.dll. renhdrum_version()
returns 0x000600, which is what src/gfx/haptic.cpp accepts; the 0.3.0 binary that this
folder held before could not load at all (its version is 0x000300 and it lacks the store,
device_classify and Xbox Direct entry points).

renhdrum.h is include/renhdrum.h from the 0.6.0 line plus the declarations the runtime
uses (Xbox Direct, adaptive triggers, Switch 2 Pro). The release asset of the same version
is sha256 664575d5a67fc52ede8a5405ecce4a925a1e96c2f985a35774e4d6ade860a621; this copy
is that file plus those declarations.

1e266ce970876c025dadba5780fde00f081c5f6dd474b9946af3cea7cbca6026  renhdrum.dll
7cc5179c4cccdcaaf6e471180419514472109cd94bf5e5c1d1d636f7ccdd5214  renhdrum.h

LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE and NOTICE are copied from the same tag: the core of
RenHDrum is dual licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0, and NOTICE asks for
"Copyright (c) 2026 Three-Dola" to be kept. The GPL-3.0-or-later parts of that
project (integrations/brontide, integrations/recomp-c/reference) are not used
here: the host calls the prebuilt library through its C ABI and does not build
any of its sources.
